# Configuration for scripts/deploy.sh (Option 2: rsync push + remote recreate).
# Copy this file to scripts/deploy.env and edit. deploy.env is git-ignored so
# host details never land in source control.
#
#     cp scripts/deploy.env.example scripts/deploy.env
#
# Every value below is optional; the script's built-in defaults match the actual
# .85 deployment (verified against /opt/stacks). Only set what differs.

# --- Docker host (the .85 server that runs the containers) ---
# DEPLOY_HOST=192.168.1.85
# DEPLOY_USER=warren               # defaults to your local username
# DEPLOY_SSH_PORT=22               # set if sshd listens on a non-standard port

# --- Dockge stacks root on the host (Dockge default is /opt/stacks) ---
# DEPLOY_STACKS_DIR=/opt/stacks

# --- Per-service mappings ---
# Each service has a bash-array of "REPO_SUBDIR::HOST_DIR" rsync mappings. The
# script runs: rsync <repo>/REPO_SUBDIR/ -> HOST_DIR/ (HOST_DIR relative to
# $DEPLOY_STACKS_DIR unless absolute). <NAME>_COMPOSE_DIR is where the remote
# `docker compose up -d --force-recreate <RECREATE_SVC>` runs.
#
# Defaults match the real host layout under /opt/stacks:
#
#   /opt/stacks/influxdb/          <- influxdb/           (compose at root)
#   /opt/stacks/grafana/           <- grafana/docker/     (compose at root)
#   /opt/stacks/provisioning/      <- grafana/provisioning/
#   /opt/stacks/dashboards/        <- grafana/dashboards/
#
# The Grafana stack on the host is "flat": its compose mounts ../provisioning and
# ../dashboards, which are SIBLING stack folders (not nested under grafana/). That
# is why grafana maps to three host folders. To change it, override here:
#
# influxdb_MAPPINGS=("influxdb::influxdb")
# influxdb_COMPOSE_DIR=influxdb
# influxdb_RECREATE_SVC=influxdb3
#
# grafana_MAPPINGS=(
#   "grafana/docker::grafana"
#   "grafana/provisioning::provisioning"
#   "grafana/dashboards::dashboards"
# )
# grafana_COMPOSE_DIR=grafana
# grafana_RECREATE_SVC=grafana
#
# osrs-current is the 5-minute catch-up ingestion daemon. Unlike the others its
# image is BUILT on the host, so the whole repo root is synced (dev-only trees
# pruned) and the compose in the nested osrsGECurrentProcess/ folder builds with
# context `..`:
#
#   /opt/stacks/osrs-current/                    <- repo root (pruned)
#   /opt/stacks/osrs-current/osrsGECurrentProcess/  compose dir (build context ..)
#
# osrs_current_MAPPINGS=(".::osrs-current")
# osrs_current_COMPOSE_DIR=osrs-current/osrsGECurrentProcess
# osrs_current_RECREATE_SVC=osrs-ge-current

# --- Ownership note (one-time host setup) ---
# The stack folders under /opt/stacks are root-owned, so rsync as your user fails
# to overwrite files. Fix once on the host so all future deploys need no sudo:
#   sudo chown -R warren:warren /opt/stacks/influxdb /opt/stacks/grafana \
#                               /opt/stacks/provisioning /opt/stacks/dashboards
